Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:33:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow: Close the interop device

InitializeDX opens a GL/Direct3D interop device with wglDXOpenDeviceNV,
which holds a reference to the D3D device until wglDXCloseDeviceNV closes
it. Nothing closed it: the destructor was defaulted. Every window kept its
D3D device alive after it was deleted, and with the device the textures
made on it, the application's own included: a process that made and
deleted DX windows grew by the device and its textures with each window.

The destructor now unregisters the shared textures and closes the interop
device with the window's context current, before the superclass
destructor deletes that context. A window whose context is gone already
(Finalize) is left as it was: its shared textures were registered with
textures of that context.
---
 Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow.cxx | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow.cxx b/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow.cxx
index b4eefed..4aeda6f 100644
--- a/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow.cxx
+++ b/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow.cxx
@@ -56,7 +56,19 @@ vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow::vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow()
 }
 
 //------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow::~vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow() = default;
+vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow::~vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow()
+{
+  // The interop device holds the D3D device, and with it the textures made on it, until it is
+  // closed. Unregister the shared textures and close it while this window's OpenGL context lives:
+  // the superclass destructor deletes the context.
+  if (this->Impl->DeviceHandle && this->ContextId)
+  {
+    this->UnregisterSharedTexture();
+    this->MakeCurrent();
+    wglDXCloseDeviceNV(this->Impl->DeviceHandle);
+    this->Impl->DeviceHandle = nullptr;
+  }
+}
 
 //------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 void vtkWin32OpenGLDXRenderWindow::SetD3DDeviceContext(ID3D11DeviceContext* context)
